<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karrani dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1564">1564</a>–<a href="/years/1576">1576</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Karrani Afghans, Karranis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Karrani dynasty was an Afghan dynasty that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> from 1564 to 1576, the last independent sultans of Bengal. Taj Khan Karrani took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaur">Gaur</a> in 1564, and his brother Sulaiman Khan Karrani moved the capital to Tanda, conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a> in 1568 and outwardly acknowledged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a>. His son Daud Khan defied the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> and was defeated and killed after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rajmahal">Battle of Rajmahal</a> in 1576.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karrani-dynasty.jpg" alt="Karrani dynasty" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Manohar, 1590 artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Da%27ud_at_the_Battle_of_Tukaroi_(3_March_1575).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
